.TH NANGER 1 "2026" "nanger 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nanger \- file manager and text editor in one (ranger + nano + vim)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nanger
.RI [ +N ] " " [ folder | file ]
.br
.B nanger \-\-init\-config | \-\-config\-path | \-\-version | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nanger
is a terminal file manager with a ranger-style three-column view and a built-in text
editor. The editor is as easy as nano (Ctrl keys, an always visible help bar) and has
vim power: regex substitution, deleting lines by pattern, sorting, shell filters, macros,
undo and redo.
.PP
Without arguments it opens the current folder. Given a folder it starts there; given a file
it opens it by type (text goes to the editor, images and PDFs to the viewer).
.B +N
opens the text file at line N.
.SH FILE MANAGER
.TP
.B Up/Down, k/j
move
.TP
.B Left, h, Backspace
parent folder
.TP
.B Right, l, Enter
enter the folder, or open the file by its type
.TP
.B s
cycle the sorting: name, size, modification time, extension
.TP
.B v
open in the built-in viewer (images and PDFs)
.TP
.B o
open with an external program (xdg-open)
.TP
.B n / N
new file / new folder
.TP
.B r
rename
.TP
.B R
bulk rename: the names open in the editor; save and close the file to apply them
.TP
.B D, Delete
delete: t = move to the trash (freedesktop trash, recoverable), d = delete permanently
(asks twice)
.TP
.B Space
mark
.TP
.B y / x / p
copy / cut / paste
.TP
.B /
search by name
.TP
.B f
search in file contents (Enter on a result opens the file at that line)
.TP
.B m / '
set a bookmark / jump to a bookmark (\(aq\(aq = previous folder, ? = list)
.TP
.B .
show hidden files
.TP
.B c
go to a path
.TP
.B b / Tab, F4
list of open files / back to the editor
.TP
.B S / !
open a shell / run a command in the current folder
.TP
.B q
quit
.SH GIT
In a git repository the file list shows the status of each entry (M modified, A added,
? untracked, D deleted, ! conflict) and the editor marks changed lines in the left margin
(+ added, ~ changed, _ lines deleted above).
.SH PREVIEW AND OPENING
The third column shows a preview: text, folder contents, archive listings (zip, tar, tar.gz,
...), and the first page of images and PDFs drawn with coloured half-blocks. This works in
any 256-colour UTF-8 terminal; no graphics protocol is needed.
.PP
Enter on a file: text \(-> editor; images, PDFs, documents (docx, odt, xlsx, ...), audio and
video \(-> the default program (xdg-open) when a graphical session exists; images and PDFs
without one (for example over SSH) \(-> the built-in viewer. In the viewer the arrows page
through the images of the folder or the pages of the PDF,
.B t
switches a PDF between text and image,
.B o
opens externally and
.B q
goes back.
.SH EDITOR
.TP
.B Ctrl+S / Ctrl+O
save / save as
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q, Ctrl+X
close
.TP
.B Ctrl+F / Ctrl+N
search / next match
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
replace (regular expression)
.TP
.B Ctrl+G
go to line
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y
undo / redo
.TP
.B Shift+arrows, Ctrl+B, Ctrl+A
selection
.TP
.B Ctrl+C / Ctrl+K / Ctrl+V
copy / cut / paste
.TP
.B Ctrl+D
duplicate the line
.TP
.B F5 / F6
record / play a macro
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
command line (see below)
.TP
.B F1
help
.SH SEVERAL OPEN FILES
Files stay open as tabs. Alt+Left/Right or Alt+1..9 switch between them; F4 or Ctrl+E goes
back to the file manager. If an open file changes on disk it is reloaded (or a warning is
shown when there are unsaved changes).
.SH COMMANDS (Ctrl+P)
.TP
.B w, q, q!, wq
save, quit, quit without saving, both
.TP
.BI % s/pattern/replacement/gi
substitute in the whole file; with a range prefix in those lines
.TP
.BI g/ pattern /d ", " v/ pattern /d
delete matching / non-matching lines
.TP
.B sort, sort!, uniq, upper, lower
sort and transform
.TP
.BI ! command
filter the selected lines through a shell command
.TP
.BI "r !" command
insert the output of a command
.TP
.BI "e " file ", e!"
open another file / reload from disk
.TP
.B ls, b N, bn, bp
list the open files, switch
.TP
.BI grep " pattern" ", copen"
search in files / show the last results
.TP
.BI @ N
play the macro N times
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B nanger \-\-init\-config
creates ~/.config/nanger/config.ini (colours, tab width, line numbers, sorting, key
remapping, language). The language is chosen with the
.B NANGER_LANG=en|hu
environment variable or the language line of the file. Bookmarks are stored in
~/.local/share/nanger/bookmarks.json.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Python 3.8 or newer. Optional:
.B Pillow
(python3-pil / python-pillow) for image and PDF previews,
.B poppler-utils
for PDFs,
.B git
for git status,
.B xdg-utils
for external opening, and
.BR wl-copy ,
.B xclip
or
.B xsel
for the system clipboard.
